    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "c7fee7aaa9eafd5dd160ce711a4ff617",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"0-load-the-potential\">0 \u00b7 Load the potential</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">First we create an ASE <strong>calculator</strong>: the object that, given atom positions, returns the energy\nand forces. With UMA it takes two lines: load the model once (a <em>predictor</em>), then wrap it in a\ncalculator for the kind of system you are simulating.</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">torch</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">fairchem.core</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">FAIRChemCalculator</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">pretrained_mlip</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">device</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"cuda\"</span> <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">torch</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cuda</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">is_available</span><span class=\"p\">()</span> <span class=\"k\">else</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"cpu\"</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># use the GPU if there is one</span>\n<span class=\"n\">predictor</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">pretrained_mlip</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get_predict_unit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"uma-s-1p2p1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">device</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">device</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">calc</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">FAIRChemCalculator</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">predictor</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"omol\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>    <span class=\"c1\"># molecules</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">UMA is one network with several <strong>task heads</strong>, one per family of training data, each matching a\ndifferent DFT setup. We use two of them:</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><code>task_name</code></th>\n<th>Trained on</th>\n<th>Used here for</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"omol\"</code></td>\n<td>molecules (\u03c9B97M-V hybrid DFT)</td>\n<td>sections 1\u20133. Needs the total <code>charge</code> and spin multiplicity <code>spin</code> in <code>atoms.info</code> (default: neutral singlet).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>\"omat\"</code></td>\n<td>inorganic crystals (PBE / PBE+U)</td>\n<td>section 4</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The notebook picks the right head automatically: periodic systems get <code>omat</code>, isolated molecules get <code>omol</code>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "PKri",
      "code_hash": "28681c8894bc2a93767418bcaeef555e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The UMA weights are free but <strong>gated</strong>: Hugging Face only lets you download them after you accept Meta's license. You only need to do this once.</span></span><marimo-accordion data-labels='[&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;paragraph&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e\ud83d\udd11 How do I get a token?&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&#92;u003c/span&#92;u003e&quot;]' data-multiple='false' data-expanded='[]'><div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><ol>\n<li>Create a free account at <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/join\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">huggingface.co/join</a> (or log in).</li>\n<li>Go to <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/facebook/UMA\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">huggingface.co/facebook/UMA</a>, fill in the form, and accept\n   the FAIR Chemistry License. <strong>Approval is manual and can take from minutes to a day or two</strong>, so do this\n   before class. You'll get an email when you're approved.</li>\n<li>Create a token at <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">huggingface.co/settings/tokens</a>:\n   <strong>Create new token \u2192 Read</strong> is enough. Copy it (it starts with <code>hf_</code>).</li>\n<li>Paste it in the box below. It stays in this session only and is not saved in the notebook.</li>\n</ol></span></div></marimo-accordion><marimo-ui-element object-id='PKri-0' random-id='66fe40f8-7381-b3d5-65b9-5a4f09032e0f'><marimo-text data-initial-value='&quot;&quot;' data-label='&quot;&#92;u003cspan class=&#92;&quot;markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents&#92;&quot;&#92;u003e&#92;u003cspan class=&#92