    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "30eb109a7c949afb3b838779e675e3c6",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"2-relax-a-real-molecule\">2 \u00b7 Relax a real molecule \ud83e\uddea</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">With <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(N||)</marimo-tex> atoms the energy depends on <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(3N||)</marimo-tex> coordinates at once, so we can no longer draw the\nlandscape. The recipe is unchanged, though, and ASE packages it into a few lines:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">ase.build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">molecule</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">ase.optimize</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">BFGS</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">atoms</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">molecule</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"H2O\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>                <span class=\"c1\"># 1. build a structure</span>\n<span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rattle</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">stdev</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">0.2</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>                <span class=\"c1\"># 2. (here) scramble it on purpose</span>\n<span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">calc</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">FAIRChemCalculator</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">predictor</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"omol\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># 3. attach UMA (molecule head)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">BFGS</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fmax</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">0.02</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>             <span class=\"c1\"># 4. step until every force &lt; 0.02 eV/\u00c5</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>fmax</code> is the <strong>convergence criterion</strong>: the run stops once the largest force on any atom drops\nbelow it. Below, we shake a molecule with random displacements and let an optimizer bring it back.\nDrag the <strong>step slider</strong> under the plots to replay the trajectory, and hover over atoms to see their forces.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
