        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><hr />\n<h2 id=\"4-relax-a-crystal\">4 \u00b7 Relax a crystal \ud83d\udc8e</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In a crystal the atoms repeat forever in a <strong>unit cell</strong>. Besides the atom positions, the\n<em>shape and size of the cell</em> can also be wrong. The cell feels a \"force\" too: the <strong>stress</strong>\n(pressure). A squeezed crystal pushes outward; a stretched one pulls inward.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">ASE lets an optimizer move the cell by wrapping the atoms in a <strong>filter</strong> that bundles the\nstress together with the atomic forces:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">ase.build</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">bulk</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">ase.filters</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">FrechetCellFilter</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">atoms</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">bulk</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Cu\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"fcc\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">3.80</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">cubic</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"kc\">True</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># deliberately strained</span>\n<span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">calc</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">FAIRChemCalculator</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">predictor</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">task_name</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"omat\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># crystal head</span>\n<span class=\"n\">BFGS</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">FrechetCellFilter</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">run</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">fmax</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">0.01</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># relax positions AND cell</span>\n<span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">atoms</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cell</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cellpar</span><span class=\"p\">())</span>                     <span class=\"c1\"># relaxed lattice constant</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Pick a crystal and strain it. Then compare relaxing <strong>atoms only</strong> with <strong>atoms + cell</strong>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
